si: A module for parsing, converting, and formatting physical quantities expressed
with the International System of Units.

- [Repository](https://codeberg.org/swonky/hare-si.git)

**Examples**

- Defining and performing arithmetic using [[quantity]]:

	const distance = si::quantity {
		unit = si::METRE,
		value = 1500.0,
	};
	const duration = si::quantity {
		unit = si::SECOND,
		value = 120.0
	};

	const speed = si::divq(distance, duration);
	assert(speed.value == 12.5);

- Defining custom [[dimension]] and [[unit]] values:

	const pressure  = dimension {
		mass = 1,
		length = -1,
		time = -2,
		...
	};
	const pascal = unit {
		dim = pressure,
		scale = 1.0,
	};
	const atmospheric_pressure  = quantity {
		unit = pascal,
		value = 101325.0,
	};

- Parsing ([[strp]]) and formatting ([[strf]]) strings:

	const qty: si::quantity = si::strp("20 m/s^2")?;
	let text: str = si::strf(qty, "km*s^-2")?;

	assert(text == "0.02 km⋅s⁻²");

	text = si::strf(
		acceleration,
		"km/s^2",
		prec=3,
		notation=si::E,
		encoding=si::ASCII,
	)?;

	assert(text == "2.00E-02 km/s^2");
